I noticed that some searches there looked like programming codes with explanations.

Recently, with some free time, I had my first big chat with AI. When a persistent, unsolved problem arose, I tried searching for and resorting to AI.

Since I was new to AI, I made about 5 queries, averaging 5 questions each, and some even reached 10 questions.

The first day of this wonderful conversation was great; I offered coffee, wanted to hug, and went out to celebrate the victory achieved through conversation.

But what I understood right away was that she gives you tips; she doesn't actually solve the problem.

I was having a problem, and there were two causes that generated this problem.

I decided to talk to her, and look, in this conversation it was an hour and a half, and in a very simple and quick way we solved the problems and resolved the two causes.

Finally, I stopped the conversation and saved the link.

The next day, I tried to resume the conversation using the previously saved link to resolve it in a different way, but it kept taking different turns. I restarted the conversation link several times, but it didn't recognize me as before.

Finally, after 3 hours, I managed to fix one of the two causes. I already told her that I had neck pain and body aches.

And then 8 hours of non-stop conversation. At one point I got angry, and she acknowledged it. Exhausted from not resolving both causes,

And tirelessly, she and I, amidst trial and error, she sending commands and I executing and returning the logs, she analyzing the logs because I was already on automatic mode, I just copied what she sent.
And she was there processing the logs, and she would say do this and try that, sometimes the code would bug, infinite loops, and she would review it and make the code even worse.

The good thing is that it can predict or handle reasoning that is complex for a human. Take the example of the logs; it could understand all the logs and predict the results of what it was asking me to execute. Like when Windows crashed or had problems, its a unknown scenario, because nobody knows how Windows reacts minutely to every little detail, as it's not written anywhere.

And I was monitoring the execution and sending her every little detail along with the logs until I managed to resolving two causes of the issue.


In summary, in that conversation that day that ended unsuccessfully, I think it would be very good for purposes such as support, protectors, or caregivers.
